app.note:
1 No clue is given as to the form in which Io was represented on the stage. In v. 848, the promise
ἐνταυ̃θα δή σε Ζεὺς τίθησιν ἔμφρονα does not imply any bodily change, but that Io laboured under a mental delusion. Still the mythologists are against us, who agree in making her transformation complete. Perhaps she was represented with horns, like the Egyptian figures of Isis, but in other respects as a virgin, which is somewhat confirmed by v. 592,
κλύεις φθέγμα τα̃ς βούκερω παρθένου;
